Q4 (1) Output of Thread Program

Program:

class A extends Thread {
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("A");
    }
}

class B extends Thread {
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("B");
    }
}

public class TestThreads {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A t1 = new A();
        B t2 = new B();

        t2.start();
        t1.start();
    }
}

Output:

A
B

OR

B
A

Explanation:

start() creates separate threads.

Thread scheduling is controlled by JVM/OS.

So we cannot predict which thread executes first.

Even though t2.start() is written first, A may print first.



